Based on my comprehensive audit of the cumulative work, I've identified one critical blocking issue:

## Issue: Pre-Existing Test Suite Failure

**Location**: `scripts/sw-code-review-test.sh:40`

**Problem**: The full `npm test` suite fails due to a cross-platform sed compatibility bug in sw-code-review-test.sh:

```bash
sed -i '' "s|\$TEST_TEMP_DIR|$TEST_TEMP_DIR|g" "$TEST_TEMP_DIR/bin/git"
```

This uses BSD sed syntax (`-i ''`) which fails on GNU sed (Linux). The error is:
```
sed: can't read s|$TEST_TEMP_DIR|/tmp/sw-test-auto.S6DBkY|g: No such file or directory
```

**Why this matters**: While the agent's work is excellent and the prebuild-validate tests pass (36/36), the full test suite (`npm test`) fails immediately when this file is sourced, preventing validation of the complete implementation.

**Note**: This is NOT a bug introduced by the agent—it's a pre-existing issue that was refactored in commit 273f154b. But it's now blocking the build.

